{"api_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/11836","collected_at":"2026-09-27T21:57:11.247406+00:00","comments":[{"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"Confirmed statically on current main; the missing gate is in the collector walk in `OptimizeThreadLocality.cpp`.\n\nThe walk accepts a reduce when: axis is the innermost dim, all operands are loads, the reduce `hasOneUse`, the update `hasOneUse`, that use is the `scf.yield`, and the init arg is a constant. What it never checks is the uses of the accumulator's region block argument. In your reproducer `acc` is read by both `tl.store(OUT...)` and the `acc + r` update, and the update itself still has exactly one use (the yield), so the walk accepts the loop.\n\nThe rewrite then re-homes the accumulator into a thread-local partial under the optimized view: the new loop carries `newAccum` (initialized by `createAccum`) and only merges the running value back after the loop in `incorporateOriginalAccumulatorValue`. The copied body keeps the `tl.store(OUT, acc)` verbatim, but `acc` now denotes the thread-local partial, so every in-loop snapshot reads the partial state (zeros at the first snapshot, partials after) while the post-loop merge still produces the correct final accumulator. That matches your log byte for byte: snapshots all 0, final correct.\n\nFix is one guard in the collector walk: the accumulator's region iter arg must have exactly one use (the update), otherwise skip the transform. I'll open the PR with a negative lit test covering the in-loop snapshot shape.\n","created_at":"2026-09-17T23:56:16Z","html_url":"https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/issues/11836#issuecomment-5722836476","id":5722836476,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/11836","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAWaHXs8AAAABVRuN_A","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/comments/5722836476/reactions"},"updated_at":"2026-09-17T23:56:16Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/comments/5722836476","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40085740?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/he-yufeng","id":40085740,"login":"he-yufeng","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMDg1NzQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng","user_view_type":"public"}}],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"author_association":"NONE","body":"### Describe the bug\n\n`TritonGPUOptimizeThreadLocality` can silently miscompile a reduction accumulator when the loop-carried accumulator is also used elsewhere inside the loop.\n\nIn the reproducer below, `acc` is stored before each update, so `OUT` should contain the running partial sums:\n\n```text\n0, 256, 512, 768\n```\n\nInstead, every snapshot is `0`, while the final accumulator is still correct.\n\n## Reproducer\n\n```python\nimport torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef kernel(X, OUT, FIN, M: tl.constexpr, K: tl.constexpr, STEPS: tl.constexpr):\n    m = tl.arange(0, M)\n    k = tl.arange(0, K)\n    acc = tl.zeros((M,), dtype=tl.float32)\n\n    for i in tl.range(0, STEPS):\n        x = tl.load(X + i * M * K + m[:, None] * K + k[None, :])\n        r = tl.sum(x, axis=1)\n\n        tl.store(OUT + i * M + m, acc)\n        acc = acc + r\n\n    tl.store(FIN + m, acc)\n\n\nM, K, STEPS = 16, 256, 4\n\nx = torch.ones((STEPS, M, K), device=\"cuda\")\nout = torch.empty((STEPS, M), device=\"cuda\")\nfin = torch.empty((M,), device=\"cuda\")\n\nkernel[(1,)](x, out, fin, M, K, STEPS, num_warps=4)\ntorch.cuda.synchronize()\n\nexpected_out = (\n    torch.arange(STEPS, device=\"cuda\", dtype=torch.float32)[:, None]\n    .expand(STEPS, M)\n    * K\n)\nexpected_fin = torch.full((M,), STEPS * K, device=\"cuda\", dtype=torch.float32)\n\nprint(\"out[:, 0]:\", out[:, 0].tolist())\nprint(\"expected :\", expected_out[:, 0].tolist())\nprint(\"final correct:\", torch.equal(fin, expected_fin))\nprint(\"snapshots correct:\", torch.equal(out, expected_out))\n```\n\nLog:\n\n```text\nout[:, 0]: [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]\nexpected : [0.0, 256.0, 512.0, 768.0]\nfinal correct: True\nsnapshots correct: False\n```\n\n## Analysis \n(By Codex,sorry for wrong)\nThe issue appears to come from: lib/Dialect/TritonGPU/Transforms/OptimizeThreadLocality.cpp\nThe reduction optimization recognizes the pattern: acc = acc + tl.sum(...) and changes it into thread-local accumulation followed by a post-loop reduction.\nThe matching logic checks that the reduction and its update have one use, but does not check whether the loop-carried accumulator block argument has additional users.\nDuring the rewrite, `createYield` changes the original accumulator to an identity-carried value:\n```cpp\nyieldValues[oldAccumBlockArgNum - 1] =\n    loop.getBody()->getArgument(oldAccumBlockArgNum);\n```\nThe actual partial accumulation is moved to a newly added loop argument.\nAs a result, additional users of the original accumulator inside the loop, such as the `tl.store` above, continue reading the identity-carried initial value (`0`) rather than the running accumulator. The post-loop result remains correct because it uses the newly introduced accumulator.\nA conservative fix may be to skip this optimization when the original accumulator block argument has uses other than the recognized update operation. \n\n### Environment details\n\nTriton: 3.8.0+git6cdc9d5\nGPU architecture: sm89","closed_at":"2026-09-21T16:55:37Z","closed_by":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13238737?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peterbell10/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peterbell10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peterbell10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peterbell10/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/peterbell10","id":13238737,"login":"peterbell10","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjM4NzM3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peterbell10/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peterbell10/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peterbell10/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peterbell10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peterbell10/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/peterbell10","user_view_type":"public"},"comments":1,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/11836/comments","created_at":"2026-09-17T16:45:17Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/11836/events","html_url":"https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/issues/11836","id":5490232614,"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"total_blocking":0},"issue_field_values":[],"labels":[{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"fc2929","default":true,"description":null,"id":125679820,"name":"bug","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMjU2Nzk4MjA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/labels/bug"}],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/trit