rl":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/he-yufeng","id":40085740,"login":"he-yufeng","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMDg1NzQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng","user_view_type":"public"},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"Confirmed statically on current main; the missing gate is in the collector walk in `OptimizeThreadLocality.cpp`.\n\nThe walk accepts a reduce when: axis is the innermost dim, all operands are loads, the reduce `hasOneUse`, the update `hasOneUse`, that use is the `scf.yield`, and the init arg is a constant. What it never checks is the uses of the accumulator's region block argument. In your reproducer `acc` is read by both `tl.store(OUT...)` and the `acc + r` update, and the update itself still has exactly one use (the yield), so the walk accepts the loop.\n\nThe rewrite then re-homes the accumulator into a thread-local partial under the optimized view: the new loop carries `newAccum` (initialized by `createAccum`) and only merges the running value back after the loop in `incorporateOriginalAccumulatorValue`. The copied body keeps the `tl.store(OUT, acc)` verbatim, but `acc` now denotes the thread-local partial, so every in-loop snapshot reads the partial state (zeros at the first snapshot, partials after) while the post-loop merge still produces the correct final accumulator. That matches your log byte for byte: snapshots all 0, final correct.\n\nFix is one guard in the collector walk: the accumulator's region iter arg must have exactly one use (the update), otherwise skip the transform. I'll open the PR with a negative lit test covering the in-loop snapshot shape.\n","created_at":"2026-09-17T23:56:16Z","event":"commented","html_url":"https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/issues/11836#issuecomment-5722836476","id":5722836476,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/11836","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAWaHXs8AAAABVRuN_A","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/comments/5722836476/reactions"},"updated_at":"2026-09-17T23:56:16Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/comments/5722836476","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40085740?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/he-yufeng","id":40085740,"login":"he-yufeng","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMDg1NzQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng","user_view_type":"public"}},{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40085740?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/he-yufeng","id":40085740,"login":"he-yufeng","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMDg1NzQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng","user_view_type":"public"},"created_at":"2026-09-18T00:02:11Z","event":"cross-referenced","source":{"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"## Summary\n\n`TritonGPUOptimizeThreadLocality` miscompiles a reduction accumulator that is also read inside the loop body (#11836). The collector walk in `OptimizeThreadLocality.cpp` gates on the reduce having one use and the update having one use, but never on the accumulator's region block argument. For a loop that reads the accumulator in its body, e.g. storing a snapshot before the update, the rewrite re-homes the accumulator into a thread-local partial under the optimized view and only merges the running value back after the loop, so every in-loop read observes the partial state instead of the running value. The reported symptom follows exactly: snapshots read zero, the final accumulator stays correct.\n\nThe fix adds one gate to the collector walk: the accumulator's region iter arg must have exactly one use (the update), otherwise the reduce is skipped.\n\n## Test plan\n\nNew negative lit test `in_loop_accumulator_use` in `test/TritonGPU/optimize-locality.mlir`: a loop that stores the accumulator in its body before the update. Without the gate the pass rewrites the loop signature and emits the `efficient_layout` view ops the checks reject; with the gate the loop, the in-loop store, and the original update survive unchanged.\n\nVerification scope, stated honestly: the mechanism above is established by reading the walk and the rewrite on current main, and the reporter's Python reproducer maps to every accepted gate (innermost axis, load operands, one-use reduce, one-use update feeding `scf.yield`, constant init). I did not execute the lit test locally: this checkout has no `triton-opt` build and producing one needs the full in-tree LLVM build, which is disproportionate for a one-line gate; the lit run is left to CI. No GPU was used at any point.\n\nCloses #11836\n","closed_at":"2026-09-21T16:55:36Z","comments":1,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/11842/comments","created_at":"2026-09-18T00:02:10Z","draft":false,"events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/11842/events","html_url":"https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/pull/11842","id":5493921010,"issue_field_values":[],"labels":[],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/11842/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":null,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAWaHXs8AAAABEAjxJw","number":11842,"performed_via_github_app":null,"pull_request":{"diff_url":"https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/pull/11842.diff","html_url":"https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/pull/11842","merged_at":"2026-09-21T16:55:36Z","patch_url":"https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/pull/11842.patch","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/pulls/11842"},"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/11842/reactions"},"repository":{"allow_forking":true,"archive_url":"https://a